  "Short answers for common setup questions.": "t-f7f3c06e723c",
  "Which versions must match?": "t-29bae6e922f0",
  "The server and every player need identical Co-op releases and the exact Bannerlord build, not just the same major version. Check release notes and the server’s refusal logs.": "t-283ea2aa1dc4",
  "Why can’t other players connect?": "t-863a38db8f15",
  "For direct connect: open the server UDP port on the host firewall and forward that same UDP port on your router. CGNAT (ISP shared public IP) can still block joins — ask for a public address or use a private network. Steam Join needs lobby mode and a logged-in Steam client; it does not fix every NAT issue.": "t-921608513c92",
  "What differs on Steam Deck, Bazzite and Flatpak Steam?": "t-7c8c3abacbeb",
  "Steam Deck: use Desktop Mode (not officially supported). Bazzite: check for Steam first — do not install a second copy. Flatpak Steam: library and permissions live in the Flatpak sandbox. Immutable hosts: prefer existing tools, Flatpak, or a tool container over changing the base OS.": "t-8cdcb5377f59",
  "Which Proton version should I choose?": "t-d6be1ad51c71",
  "Use the Co-op release’s recommended Proton/GE build, or one already known to run Bannerlord. Find the real proton executable — paths vary. Stock Wine 8 failed headless SERVING here; WineHQ Wine 11.0 + Xvfb was validated. Wine 9/10 and umu are untested here. Do not break a working game install just to try the server.": "t-54f9e875e7b5",
  "Why does the server close or crash?": "t-7038d13548d4",
  "Read terminal output and dedicated-server logs first. Check exact game/Co-op builds, extraction and runtime paths. Exit code 25 points to starter_log.txt under ProgramData/Mount and Blade II Bannerlord/logs. Never delete saves as a shortcut.": "t-9c3a91fe3d2f",
  "Can Workshop auto-updates break joining?": "t-f75bffdbf5e9",
  "Yes. Workshop can update the client before the server, or lag because releases need TaleWorlds approval. Compare exact builds and restore a compatible pair. Restart Steam only when safe for active sessions; this guide does not change subscriptions.": "t-60ce7da277f8",
  "Does the server need a GPU or display?": "t-dd8e6b93c80c",
  "A dedicated server does not need a running Bannerlord game instance. GPU/display-free Proton operation on every VPS is still unverified. Steam lobby mode needs a logged-in Steam client; direct-IP mode is separate.": "t-71605b42750e",
  "How do I update safely?": "t-d5339d320eea",
  "Save cleanly and stop only the intended server. Back up its entire CoopData directory and any separate server-data folder before changing files. Extract the update separately, retain configuration and saves, match client/game builds, then verify startup.": "t-d49b6d828caf",
  "How do I keep it running?": "t-abb60a76712b",
  "After a successful manual start, wrap the same command in a user systemd service. Check logs with journalctl --user -u YOUR_UNIT. OpenRC/runit templates vary by distro and are unverified. Never reuse a live production unit for a test.": "t-e5ba846098be",
  "Where are logs and saves?": "t-3861ff808250",
  "Under Proton, inspect the selected prefix’s drive_c/users/steamuser/Documents/Mount and Blade II Bannerlord/CoopData/DedicatedServer. Logs are under logs/ and saves under Game Saves/. Confirm the paths printed at boot; --data-dir can change them. Back up before editing.": "t-c1770853cf81",
  "Where is the dedicated-server download?": "t-559fb838d1e6",
  "Use the release changelog and manifest. The Win64 .7z is distributed on the Co-op CDN and may be absent from GitHub Assets. SteamCMD is not a substitute for this archive.": "t-d915cae4f42e",
  "Does disabling the watchdog help Linux stutter?": "t-ba74354481b0",
  "Official Discord reports say it can help. Rename the client watchdog directory rather than deleting it, and keep a backup. Developer caveat: crash logs are then unavailable for support. --no-watchdog is server-only. Do not change a running game.": "t-872609587be3",
  "Can I use the Workshop dedicated server?": "t-42f13b13a772",
  "Yes: the Workshop item includes DedicatedServer. Steam keeps Workshop on the latest approved release automatically, but TaleWorlds approval can lag GitHub/CDN. The host and every player must still match. Manual Modules/Coop and Workshop Co-op must not be enabled together.": "t-2e0973f456af",
  "Which ports should direct-IP players allow?": "t-f2b6e4497570",
  "Official Discord recommends UDP 4200–4201 through host, router and cloud firewall with steam:false. Steam player-hosted invites can bypass forwarding, but dedicated-server Steam listing under Proton/Wine remains unverified here.": "t-4f4c120eefd2",
  "Why is the service running but there is no UDP listener?": "t-c52751ba2f3e",
  "A new server often waits for an interactive EULA answer before binding the port. Read EULA.md and LICENSE.txt, accept only if you agree, then start the service and confirm a SERVING log line. Do not automate consent or copy another server’s acceptance file.": "t-116b17f95200",
  "Is Linux or Steam Deck supported?": "t-4cecec659833",
  "The official FAQ states that Linux is supported but Steam Deck is not. Deck reports vary; see issue #2162. This is a Linux setup guide.": "t-eef36cbdc0c8",
  "What if I host and play on the same PC?": "t-900bddaacdf3",
  "The official FAQ suggests an 8-core CPU and 16 GB RAM. Linux host-and-play can stall during character transfer (issue #2095). A separate dedicated server may help; this guide does not promise a fix.": "t-a825692972b4",
  "Where are difficulty and battle settings?": "t-61097f6242ac",
  "Check CoopData/mod-config.json; server connection settings are in CoopData/DedicatedServer/server-config.json. Stop the intended server before editing. Lower battleSize for battle performance; back up before regenerating a config with missing options.": "t-21513f8cb5b1",
  "Can Epic or manually installed clients use Steam invites?": "t-3d9fda7f4129",
  "Steam lobbies are Steam-to-Steam. Epic and non-Steam distributions need Direct IP with the configured UDP port, or an appropriate private network. Everyone still needs identical game and Co-op builds.": "t-81e45120bdf3",
  "Do client and server versions match?": "t-bcff40a42336",
  "They must. The staging resolver downloads matching client and dedicated-server assets from one release. Compare Modules/Coop/SubModule.xml with the server release tag (RESOLVED_VERSION.txt). The script warns when they differ.": "t-1c1eea4ef518",
  "Can I use an AI assistant?": "t-f7062606e4c3",
  "An AI assistant can help explain this guide, but it may miss Bannerlord-specific details or suggest incorrect fixes. Check commands against the guide before running them.": "t-07ead78d148d",
  "Self-contained AI prompt": "t-6fbb40b51084",
